    <!-- Page title card -->
    <section class="glass-card-display hero-introduction" id="hero-section">
        <div class="card-header-centered">
            <h2>CORTEX — Business Leader View</h2>
        </div>
        <p class="hero-description">
            AI-powered engineering governance that <strong>pays for itself</strong>.
            CORTEX eliminates rework, prevents defects before they ship, optimises LLM token spend,
            and delivers measurable velocity gains — turning your engineering investment into
            predictable, auditable output, sprint after sprint.
        </p>
        <div class="hero-stats">
            <span class="stat-pill">4× Faster Root Cause Resolution</span>
            <span class="stat-pill">Precision LLM Token Use</span>
            <span class="stat-pill">Zero Governance Violations in Production</span>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
         CONTENT
         ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
    <div class="role-content-wrapper">

        <!-- ════════════════════════════════════════════════
             SECTION 1 — BOTTOM LINE
             One punchy statement before any numbers.
             ════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
        <div class="bl-section-panel">
            <div class="bl-bottom-line">
                <h3 class="bl-bottom-line-heading">Every engineering defect found in production costs 10–100× more to fix than one caught at commit. CORTEX makes catching it at commit the default — automatically, on every change, without slowing your team down.</h3>
                <p class="bl-bottom-line-body">
                    CORTEX is a production-grade AI Engineering Framework that enforces quality governance at the source.
                    <strong>99 consecutive delivery phases.</strong>
                    <strong>32 governance rules</strong> enforced automatically across 8 pipeline stages — no manual review gates, no spreadsheet compliance.
                    The result: predictable velocity, observable quality, and audit-ready compliance from day one.
                    This page builds your understanding systematically: <strong>Problem → Solution → Proof → Strategic Value</strong>.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div><!-- /.bl-section-panel: Bottom Line -->

        <!-- ════════════════════════════════════════════════
             SECTION 2 — THE PROBLEM: Cost of Unmanaged AI
             D3 bar chart comparing defect discovery costs
             ════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
        <div class="bl-section-panel">
            <h2 class="role-section-title"><i class="fas fa-exclamation-triangle"></i> The Problem: Defects Get Exponentially More Expensive</h2>

            <p class="bl-tab-desc">Every stage a defect travels through your pipeline multiplies the cost to fix it. AI tooling without governance accelerates defect <em>velocity</em>, not just feature velocity. The chart below shows why catching issues earlier is a financial imperative, not a quality preference.</p>

            <!-- D3.js: Cost-of-defect bar chart -->
            <div class="bl-d3-panel" id="defect-cost-chart" role="img" aria-label="Bar chart showing relative cost of defect discovery by stage">
                <div class="bl-d3-title">Relative Cost of Defect Discovery by Stage</div>
                <div class="bl-d3-subtitle">Index: 1× = caught at commit · Higher = more expensive to fix · Reference: NIST, IBM Systems Sciences Institute</div>
                <div class="bl-d3-canvas" id="defect-cost-canvas"></div>
                <div class="bl-d3-legend">
                    <span class="bl-d3-legend-item bl-d3-legend--green"><span class="bl-d3-legend-dot"></span>CORTEX blocks here (pre-commit)</span>
                    <span class="bl-d3-legend-item bl-d3-legend--amber"><span class="bl-d3-legend-dot"></span>Internal discovery</span>
                    <span class="bl-d3-legend-item bl-d3-legend--red"><span class="bl-d3-legend-dot"></span>Production exposure</span>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="bl-insight-row">
                <div class="bl-insight-card bl-insight-card--green">
                    <div class="bl-insight-icon"><i class="fas fa-shield-alt"></i></div>
                    <div class="bl-insight-text"><strong>CORTEX blocks defects at commit</strong> — before they enter the review cycle. The enforcement gate runs in &lt;10 seconds on every change, coordinated by 10 specialised agents.</div>
                </div>
                <div class="bl-insight-card bl-insight-card--red">
                    <div class="bl-insight-icon"><i class="fas fa-fire"></i></div>
                    <div class="bl-insight-text"><strong>Without governance</strong>, AI-generated code compounds the problem — higher feature velocity into a higher defect rate at the same late-stage discovery cost.</div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div><!-- /.bl-section-panel: The Problem -->

        <!-- ════════════════════════════════════════════════
             SECTION 3 — THE SOLUTION: How CORTEX Works
             Mermaid: request flow pipeline
             ════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
        <div class="bl-section-panel">
            <h2 class="role-section-title"><i class="fas fa-cogs"></i> How CORTEX Works: The 8-Stage Pipeline</h2>

            <p class="bl-tab-desc">Every engineering action — from a code change to a debug request — flows through 8 automated stages. No human gates required. Governance is infrastructure, not process.</p>

            <!-- Mermaid: pipeline flow -->
            <div class="bl-mermaid-panel" aria-label="CORTEX 8-stage governance pipeline diagram">
                <div class="bl-mermaid-title"><i class="fas fa-project-diagram"></i> Request → Quality-Assured Output</div>
                <div class="bl-mermaid-canvas">
                    <pre class="mermaid">
flowchart LR
    A["🔧 Code Change\nor AI Request"] --> B["⚡ Request\nEnrichment\nStage -1"]
    B --> C["🌐 MCP\nGateway\nStage 0"]
    C --> D["🎯 Intent\nClassifier\n29 Types"]
    D --> E["🔬 LENS\nAnalysis\n300-800ms"]
    E --> F["🧠 Brain\nIntelligence\n50-200ms"]
    F --> G{"🛡️ Governance\nGate\n10 Agents"}
    G -->|"✅ PASS"| H["⚙️ TDD\nExecution\nRED→GREEN"]
    G -->|"🚫 BLOCKED"| I["❌ Rejected\nNo tokens\nspent"]
    H --> J["📊 SQLite\nAudit Trail\nAC markers"]

    classDef stage fill:#0d1b3e,stroke:#00d4ff,stroke-width:1.5px,color:#e2e8f0
    classDef gate fill:#0d2b1e,stroke:#34d399,stroke-width:2px,color:#34d399
    classDef block fill:#2d0f0f,stroke:#fb7185,stroke-width:1.5px,color:#fb7185
    classDef audit fill:#1a0d3d,stroke:#7b61ff,stroke-width:1.5px,color:#a78bfa
    classDef input fill:#1a1a2e,stroke:#a0a6c0,stroke-width:1.5px,color:#e2e8f0

    class A input
    class B,C,D,E,F stage
    class G gate
    class H stage
    class I block
    class J audit
                    </pre>
                </div>
                <p class="bl-mermaid-caption">Every change is enriched, classified, analysed, and governance-gated before execution. Blocked requests consume zero engineering time and zero LLM tokens.</p>
            </div>

            <!-- Pipeline detail cards -->
            <div class="bl-section-divider">
                <div class="bl-section-divider-line"></div>
                <span class="bl-section-divider-label">8-Stage Detail</span>
                <div class="bl-section-divider-line"></div>
            </div>
            <div class="bl-pipeline-grid">

                <div class="bl-pipeline-card bl-pipeline-card--cyan">
                    <div class="bl-pipeline-card-header">
                        <span class="bl-pipeline-badge bl-pipeline-badge--cyan">−1</span>
                        <i class="fas fa-filter bl-pipeline-icon bl-pipeline-icon--cyan"></i>
                    </div>
                    <div class="bl-pipeline-card-title">Request Enrichment</div>
                    <div class="bl-pipeline-card-desc">Silent pre-processing adds governance context, breaking-risk assessment, and design pillar considerations before the request reaches any orchestrator.</div>
                </div>

                <div class="bl-pipeline-card bl-pipeline-card--cyan">
                    <div class="bl-pipeline-card-header">
                        <span class="bl-pipeline-badge bl-pipeline-badge--cyan">0</span>
                        <i class="fas fa-network-wired bl-pipeline-icon bl-pipeline-icon--cyan"></i>
                    </div>
                    <div class="bl-pipeline-card-title">MCP Gateway</div>
                    <div class="bl-pipeline-card-desc">JSON-RPC 2.0 over stdio validates the request, routes to the correct MCP tool from 30 registered tools, and enforces rate limiting.</div>
                </div>

                <div class="bl-pipeline-card bl-pipeline-card--violet">
                    <div class="bl-pipeline-card-header">
                        <span class="bl-pipeline-badge bl-pipeline-badge--violet">1</span>
                        <i class="fas fa-crosshairs bl-pipeline-icon bl-pipeline-icon--violet"></i>
                    </div>
                    <div class="bl-pipeline-card-title">Intent Classification</div>
                    <div class="bl-pipeline-card-desc">IntentRouter classifies across 29 intent types. High confidence routes immediately; low confidence requests clarification before any code is touched.</div>
                </div>

                <div class="bl-pipeline-card bl-pipeline-card--violet">
                    <div class="bl-pipeline-card-header">
                        <span class="bl-pipeline-badge bl-pipeline-badge--violet">2</span>
                        <i class="fas fa-microscope bl-pipeline-icon bl-pipeline-icon--violet"></i>
                    </div>
                    <div class="bl-pipeline-card-title">LENS Analysis</div>
                    <div class="bl-pipeline-card-desc">Parallel analyzers scan AST structure, Git history, security vulnerabilities, architecture patterns, and complexity metrics simultaneously — sub-second.</div>
                    <div class="bl-pipeline-card-timing">300–800 ms</div>
                </div>

                <div class="bl-pipeline-card bl-pipeline-card--emerald">
                    <div class="bl-pipeline-card-header">
                        <span class="bl-pipeline-badge bl-pipeline-badge--emerald">3</span>
                        <i class="fas fa-brain bl-pipeline-icon bl-pipeline-icon--emerald"></i>
                    </div>
                    <div class="bl-pipeline-card-title">Brain Intelligence</div>
                    <div class="bl-pipeline-card-desc">Perception recognises patterns, Reasoning selects strategies by historical success rate, Action builds a TDD-gated execution plan with rollback points.</div>
                    <div class="bl-pipeline-card-timing">50–200 ms</div>
                </div>

                <div class="bl-pipeline-card bl-pipeline-card--emerald">
                    <div class="bl-pipeline-card-header">
                        <span class="bl-pipeline-badge bl-pipeline-badge--emerald">4</span>
                        <i class="fas fa-shield-alt bl-pipeline-icon bl-pipeline-icon--emerald"></i>
                    </div>
                    <div class="bl-pipeline-card-title">Governance Gate</div>
                    <div class="bl-pipeline-card-desc">EnforcementOrchestrator coordinates 10 specialised agents — GovernanceAgent, SecurityAgent, ComplianceAgent, FileNamingAgent, ArchitectureIntegrityAgent, and 5 more.</div>
                    <div class="bl-pipeline-card-result">
                        <span class="bl-pipeline-result bl-pipeline-result--pass">PASS</span>
                        <span class="bl-pipeline-result bl-pipeline-result--warn">WARNING</span>
                        <span class="bl-pipeline-result bl-pipeline-result--block">BLOCKED</span>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="bl-pipeline-card bl-pipeline-card--amber">
                    <div class="bl-pipeline-card-header">
                        <span class="bl-pipeline-badge bl-pipeline-badge--amber">5</span>
                        <i class="fas fa-vial bl-pipeline-icon bl-pipeline-icon--amber"></i>
                    </div>
                    <div class="bl-pipeline-card-title">TDD Execution</div>
                    <div class="bl-pipeline-card-desc">TDDOrchestrator writes failing tests first, then minimum implementation, then improves quality — all tests must stay green. CORE-008 is architecturally mandated.</div>
                    <div class="bl-pipeline-card-tdd">
                        <span class="bl-tdd-badge bl-tdd-red">RED</span>
                        <i class="fas fa-arrow-right bl-tdd-arrow"></i>
                        <span class="bl-tdd-badge bl-tdd-green">GREEN</span>
                        <i class="fas fa-arrow-right bl-tdd-arrow"></i>
                        <span class="bl-tdd-badge bl-tdd-blue">REFACTOR</span>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="bl-pipeline-card bl-pipeline-card--rose">
                    <div class="bl-pipeline-card-header">
                        <span class="bl-pipeline-badge bl-pipeline-badge--rose">6</span>
                        <i class="fas fa-database bl-pipeline-icon bl-pipeline-icon--rose"></i>
                    </div>
                    <div class="bl-pipeline-card-title">Audit Trail — SQLite WAL</div>
                    <div class="bl-pipeline-card-desc">Every action logs AC_START and AC_COMPLETE timestamps to CortexAuditDB with hash-chain integrity. Auditors get queryable evidence — not spreadsheet archaeology.</div>
                </div>

            </div>
        </div><!-- /.bl-section-panel: How CORTEX Works -->

        <!-- ════════════════════════════════════════════════
             SECTION 4 — QUANTIFIED IMPACT (ROI Grid)
             ════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
        <div class="bl-section-panel">
            <h2 class="role-section-title"><i class="fas fa-chart-line"></i> Proof: Quantified Business Impact</h2>

            <p class="bl-tab-desc">These outcomes are observable in this codebase today — not projections. Every metric is backed by 99 consecutive delivery phases with a full queryable audit trail.</p>
            <div class="roi-grid">
                <div class="roi-card">
                    <div class="roi-icon">🧪</div>
                    <div class="roi-value">Shift Left</div>
                    <div class="roi-label">Defect Detection</div>
