                    <strong>Defects from non-compliant code</strong> — blocked at commit by 10 enforcement agents before they reach a reviewer. <strong>Rework from vague acceptance criteria</strong> — DoR enforcement requires a testable definition before any work begins. <strong>Security issues discovered post-ship</strong> — LENS scans for CVEs, insecure patterns, and PHI/PII exposure during planning, not after deployment. <strong>Recurring failures</strong> — RCA prevention rules written to the governance registry mean the same root cause cannot silently recur. <strong>Governance audit overhead</strong> — 32 CORE rules enforced automatically at pre-commit and CI, with a queryable SQLite audit trail, eliminating manual compliance reviews. The magnitude of savings depends on your team's baseline defect rate, sprint cost, and audit cadence — CORTEX provides the mechanisms; the return scales with your context.
